{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/{acceptance,acceptance-browser,dist,acceptance-node}.report.md'","aggregated_output":"<!-- Author: Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort xhigh (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ecaf-0fdc-7631-a7e1-58ed8c0b7479). -->\n\nBuilt the [acceptance matrix](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/matrix.json) with 61 criteria and 35 chart-type rules, a dependency-free [checker](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/check.mjs), fixture tests, and a [README](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/README.md).\n\nThe [report](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/report.md) records **13 pass, 0 fail, 251 no evidence, 25 not run, 21 cannot be verified here, and 266 not applicable** after joining the latest unit results.\n\n**Highest-priority gaps**\n\n1. **Data fidelity.** F2 and F3 have only partial evidence across all six chart types. F12 still needs changed-value disclosures verified in the accessibility tree and in production. F10 lacks complete stack coverage for area, bar, and compact. F8 lacks end-to-end coverage for donut edge cases.\n2. **Accessible reading.** A1 and A5 lack full evidence for every type. A2 has partial keyboard evidence, and A4 has line browser coverage awaiting execution and gaps for area, bar, scatter, and donut. A3 requires screen-reader rehearsal.\n3. **Legibility and interaction.** L8 lacks full fallback evidence for all five full chart types. I1 lacks end-to-end pointer evidence across those same types, including the p95 latency check. Compact C1–C4 have partial evidence. A9 still needs the published WCAG conformance table.\n\nThe [prioritized gap list](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/acceptance/report.md:120) names every affected chart type and explains what each weak test leaves unchecked.\n\n**Verified.** The checker exited `0` with and without the Vitest report. `--release` exited `1` on coverage gaps. The six checker cases passed.\n\n```text\nℹ tests 6\nℹ pass 6\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\nThe latest Vitest run recorded 590 passing assertions, a normalization timing failure at 125.2 ms against a 100 ms threshold, and a palette suite that could not load `research/palette/palette.json`. Those failures are recorded separately from acceptance-cell results. Browser tests were not run.\n\nSection 3.6 cells that say “No” are checks of feature absence. Archived benchmark measurements are linked without verdicts while limits remain provisional. No contract changes are needed.<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a61d95e46b3f0f3aa. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Browser acceptance suite: report\n\nI wrote 457 browser tests under `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/`. On the default SVG renderer, 443 pass and 14 fail. Each failure is either a spec point the build does not meet or a reading of an ambiguous sentence that I marked \"(reading: …)\" in the title. Nothing outside my directory was edited and nothing was committed. `tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit` reports no errors in my files.\n\n**The build changed under me.** Other agents rebuilt `dist` at 06:14 and 06:20 and kept editing `src` (`dom/tooltip.ts`, `dom/interaction.ts`, `dom/figure.ts`, `theme/css.ts`, `dom/table.ts`). Before the final run I ran `npm run build` myself. The final run started at 06:21:31.\n\nSome results moved between builds:\n- **Started passing:** single-click Pan buttons (I3), a visible \"Jump to\" error (A4), the note staying in the figure (F12 bar), the A7 position-text test, the dark-scheme palette.\n- **Changed how it fails:** the I1 bar test. It first failed because pointing at the plot's bottom row showed nothing; now it fails because the tooltip leaves the viewport at the top edge.\n- **Gaps you listed that now pass:** pan buttons and the jump error.\n- **One gap not tested:** category-axis zoom being off is the spec's own rule (\"on time, date and numeric x only\"); the T-zoom-bar test checks exactly that and passes.\n\n### Files\n- Tests: `a1-names`, `a2-keyboard`, `a4-table`, `a5-not-colour-alone`, `a6-a10`, `f12-note`, `f8-donut`, `f2-gaps`, `l-legibility`, `i1-pointer` (I1–I6), `type-matrix`, `compact` (each `.browser.test.ts`).\n- Helpers:\n  - `util.ts`: pages, the accessibility tree via CDP, tab stops, shape and colour readers.\n  - `fixtures.ts`: hand-written data and expected text, plus copies of `dirty`, `bars` and `parts`.\n  - `text.ts`: rotated text boxes and a 1 px overlap test.\n  - `vision.ts`: OKLab and Machado 2009 colour-vision simulation.\n  - `prod.html`: the minified production bundle.\n- `EVIDENCE.json`: 457 entries, one per test, built from the Vitest JSON report.\n- Scratch files are removed.\n\n### Test counts (ran and saw, final run)\n| Criterion | Tests per type (failing in brackets) |\n|---|---|\n| A1 | line 8, area 8, bar 8, scatter 8, donut 7, compact 7 |\n| A2 | line 9, area 9, bar 8, scatter 8, donut 6 |\n| A4 | line 6, area 5, bar 4, scatter 5, donut 4 |\n| A5 | line 7, area 7, bar 5 (1), scatter 4, donut 4, compact 6 |\n| A6 (Chrome only) | 2 each for line, area, bar, scatter, donut |\n| A7 | 3 each for line, area, bar, scatter; donut 2 |\n| A8 | 1 per type, including compact; each test covers every state |\n| A10 | 2 per type (1 failing in each) |\n| F12 | line, area, bar, scatter 5 each; donut 6 |\n| F8 | donut 6 |\n| F2 | line 3, area 3, compact 2, bar 2, scatter 1, donut 1 |\n| L1 | 3 per type (line, area, scatter and donut each 1 failing) |\n| L2, L4, L7 | 2, 3 and 2 per type, compact included |\n| L3, L8 | 3 and 2 per full type |\n| L5 | line 1, area 1 |\n| L6 | 2 each for line, area, bar, scatter; donut 1 |\n| I1 | line 4, area 4, bar 4 (1), scatter 3 (1), donut 2 |\n| I2 | 1 each for line, area, bar, scatter |\n| I3 | 5 each for line, area, bar, scatter |\n| I4 | 2 per full type |\n| I5 | 3 per type, compact included |\n| I6 | 1 per full type |\n| T-pointer, T-tooltip, T-keyboard, T-zoom, T-dense, T-limit, T-reference | 1 per applicable type each |\n| C1 / C2 / C3 / C4 / C5 | 12 / 5 / 3 / 3 (1) / 3 |\n\n### Failing tests (ran and saw)\n1. **A10, all 6 types: the summary is not marked `lang=\"en\"` on a `lang=\"de\"` page.**\n   - Spec: \"Built-in English text is marked lang=\"en\" when the document language is not English.\"\n   - Expected (reading): the generated summary sentences are built-in English and should be marked.\n   - Page: `.axylo-summary` has no English `lang` ancestor. The note, toolbar, plot and pager are marked correctly.\n   - Likely cause: `src/dom/figure.ts` `update()` sets `lang` only on the note and the message, and `FigureModel` has no summary language field.\n2. **A5 bar: grouped bars touch.**\n   - Spec: \"Adjacent filled marks … are separated by at least 1 px of background.\"\n   - Page: the two bars of a group touch; background coverage between them is 0.22 px.\n   - Likely cause: `src/scene/bars.ts` lines 71–75, where `width = part`, so there is no gap inside a group.\n   - Reading: grouped bars count as adjacent filled marks, although the spec only names slices and stacked segments.\n3. **C4 compact bar: two compact bar series differ by colour only.**\n   - Page: both series draw with dash `none`, no fill pattern and no other cue.\n   - Reading: C4 names lines; I applied \"never by colour alone\" (A5) to bars.\n   - Likely cause: `src/scene/bars.ts` and the compact cue logic in `src/view` give compact bars no cue.\n4. **L1, line, area, scatter and donut, 200 % text only.**\n   - Spec: zero text outside the figure.\n   - Page: at 240 and 320 px wide (360 px tall), the chart falls back to the too-small state (L8). It shows the whole multi-sentence summary, which overflows the figure, and \"View as table\" ends up outside it. On the donut, the legend list overflows too. With plain text and with the WCAG text-spacing overrides, all widths pass.\n   - Likely cause: `src/dom/figure.ts` (`summaryVisible`) shows the full summary, while L8 asks for a one-line summary.\n5. **I1 scatter: one point cannot be picked.**\n   - Setup: a full-viewport chart (body margin 0, chart 100vw × 100vh). The point EU (20 kB, 140 ms) sits on the plot's top edge and shares x with US (20, 100).\n   - Page: pointing exactly at it, or 10–12 px away, shows neither a tooltip nor the readout. The same point is pickable in the default 720 × 400 layout.\n   - Likely cause: `src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts` (`pick`, its row/column edge handling). Not confirmed.\n6. **I1 bar: the tooltip leaves the viewport.**\n   - Spec: the tooltip \"stays inside the viewport\".\n   - Page: pointing at the top edge of the plot in a full-viewport chart puts the tooltip partly outside the viewport, at all 7 columns.\n   - Likely cause: `src/dom/tooltip.ts` placement, which was being edited during the run.\n\n### Not covered, and why\n- **Cannot be verified here:** A3 with a real screen reader, A6 in Firefox and Safari, phone behaviour for I4, GPU rasterisation. A6 and I4 were run in Chrome only, with emulated touch.\n- **L1 with a late-loading font:** no font file is available offline.\n- **I5 \"24-chart filter change settles within 200 ms\":** a timing budget, so it is left out.\n- **A9:** a document, not a browser test.\n- **Node side:** F1, F3–F7, F9–F11, DX and P are left to the Node suite. F5 has only its rendered half here (T-dense-line and T-dense-area).\n- **Canvas renderer:** not run; the known canvas separator gap is therefore not exercised.\n- **Note text and placement:** these tests rely on a `waitForFunction` wait. It gives the note time to appear and then asserts on it.\n\n### Spec ambiguities and the reading chosen\n| Topic | Reading |\n|---|---|\n| Value format | Number, a space, then the unit (\"12 kWh\"). Dates use the en-US medium form. |\n| Summary \"y range\" | The data's minimum to maximum, not the axis. |\n| Scatter \"last\" | The point with the largest x. |\n| Donut summary | Each slice's value and share. |\n| Table jump field | WCAG 3.3.1 applies: an unmatched value needs visible error text. |\n| Separators | Anti-aliased background coverage summed between the two marks is at least 0.75 px. A rect geometry check is added for stacked bars. |\n| Grayscale A5 | Binarised last-point markers overlap by at most 85 % of their union, at DPR 2. |\n| A7 | A focused range whose value text changes is spoken, so its position must not count arriving rows. This now passes. |\n| F12 \"changed\" | An AX160 formatter fallback counts as a changed value; AX121 grouping does too. |\n| L1 200 % text-only zoom | Twice the inherited font size. |\n| Tooltip hover (WCAG 1.4.13) | The pointer moves onto the tooltip in one step. With a slow sweep the content follows the pointer on nearest-x charts. |\n| Scatter zoom \"x only\" | The y domain is unchanged after an x zoom. |\n| I5 slack | Settled 300 ms after an update (200 ms plus 100 ms of slack). |\n\n### Last lines of the final run (default renderer, ran and saw)\n```\n Test Files  5 failed | 7 passed (12)\n      Tests  14 failed | 443 passed (457)\n   Start at  06:21:31\n   Duration  221.13s (tests 99%, import 1%)\n```\nRun with `npm run build` then `AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance`.\n<!-- Author: Claude Opus 5.5 (requested effort high), Agent-tool subagent a6f0d7846bf125638. Saved by the coordinator from the hand-back. -->\n\n## Distribution tests for Axylo (M7: DX1, DX7, DX8, DX11): report\n\nAll 101 distribution tests pass against the packed tarballs. The size targets do not: the line-only and everything bundles are about 98 KiB gzipped, against 25 and 40 KiB. I did not commit anything.\n\n**Library state for the final run.** HEAD was `43fc75d`, plus another agent's uncommitted changes in `packages/axylo/src` (core, dom, render, theme, view). My `node scripts/pack.mjs` rebuilt dist at 06:54 CET. The last test and size runs were at 06:55 CET.\n\n### Files\n\nNew:\n- `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/pack.mjs`: root build (unless `--no-build`), `npm pack` of both packages into `tests/dist/.packed/`, then a built-in tar extractor unpacks them into the fixture `node_modules`. `react`, `react-dom` and `@types/react*` are linked from the root `node_modules`; `axylo` and `@axylo/react` are never linked.\n- `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/examples/first-chart/npm.ts`, `script.html`, `react.tsx`: 8, 10 and 10 non-blank lines.\n- `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/`:\n  - test config and helpers: `vitest.config.ts` (its global setup packs before every run), `setup.ts`, `tsconfig.json`, `paths.ts`, `browser.ts` (my own HTTP server, see below), `README.md`\n  - Node tests: `isolation`, `package-contents`, `types`, `conditions`, `side-effects`, `node`, `licence`, `snippets` (`*.test.ts`)\n  - browser tests: `first-chart.browser.test.ts`, `csp.browser.test.ts`\n  - pages: `pages/{observe.js, page.css, charts.ts, inject.js}`\n  - fixtures: `fixtures/{npm,script,react}/` with `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, consumer files, `node-import.mjs`, `main.tsx`, `hydrate.tsx`, `ssr.tsx`\n- `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/LICENSE`, `packages/react/LICENSE` (MIT, holder \"The Axylo authors\": please confirm), both READMEs (they quote the example files verbatim, and a test enforces that), `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`.\n\nRewritten: `/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs`.\n\nI did not reuse `packages/axylo/test/browser/harness.ts`: it serves the whole repository with no response headers.\n\n### Metadata changes I made, each driven by a failing test\n- **`files` in `packages/axylo/package.json`:** narrowed from `[\"dist\"]` to the 5 JS/CSS files plus `index.d.ts` and `public.d.ts`. Before, the tarball shipped 96 files, 87 of them internal `.d.ts` files that nothing imports. It now ships 10.\n- **`files` in `packages/react/package.json`:** narrowed to `index.js`, `index.dev.js` and `index.d.ts`. `patch.d.ts` is not imported by `index.d.ts`.\n- **`sideEffects` in `packages/axylo/package.json`:** changed from `false` to `[\"*.css\"]`, because `false` was untrue for `axylo/axylo.css`. esbuild keeps the CSS import either way. The reason is webpack's documented rule for CSS imports; I could not test it because webpack is not installed.\n\n### What ran (all observed)\n- Node, `npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`: `Test Files 8 passed (8) / Tests 83 passed (83)`.\n- Browser, `AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`: `Test Files 2 passed (2) / Tests 18 passed (18)`.\n- `npx tsc -p tests/dist`: exit 0.\n- `packages/react/test/dist.test.ts`: still 12/12 after the metadata changes.\n\nWhat each group shows:\n- **Isolation:** the fixture packages are real directories, not links. Node (with and without `--conditions=development`) and esbuild resolve `axylo`, `axylo/axylo.css`, `@axylo/react`, and the adapter's own `import 'axylo'`, to fixture paths only. A control assertion confirms the root `node_modules/axylo` really does link to the workspace, so the check has something to catch.\n- **Package contents:** every `exports` target under every condition, and every `files` entry, is in the tarball. Nothing else ships beyond the declarations the types entries import, the two IIFE files, README, LICENSE and package.json. No source, tests or source maps; declarations import only peer dependencies.\n- **Types:** strict `tsc` with `skipLibCheck: false` passes on a consumer file and on each snippet, in both fixtures. `--listFiles` shows the declarations came from the fixture. The `@ts-expect-error` lines for the DX3 mistakes behave correctly, so the declarations are real types, not `any`.\n- **Conditions:** `development` and the default are different files in Node and in esbuild, and neither contains `__DEV__`.\n  - How I checked for development-only code: I found every `if (__DEV__) …` in the source and bundled the source twice, once as is and once with those statements cut out. Text present only in the first bundle counts as development-only.\n  - Found for `axylo`: `__dev`, `stages`, `retainedRows`. For `@axylo/react`: `[axylo/react] <`, `> was given `, `columns`.\n  - Each is present in the packed development file and absent from the production one.\n  - In the browser, the AX104 hint prints once in the development flavour and not at all in production.\n- **Side effects:** importing either package and using nothing bundles to 0 bytes. Importing `axylo` in Node adds no globals, and in Chrome it leaves the document untouched. `import 'axylo/axylo.css'` survives bundling.\n- **DX8 in Node:**\n  - Importing `axylo` works without DOM globals.\n  - `validate()` on the Phase 1 dirty fixture returns exactly AX102 (row 5), AX103 (row 3) and AX106 (row 4), as spec 3.5 and plan 1.6 say.\n  - `line('#nowhere')` with no document throws a message naming `#nowhere`.\n  - Server rendering of the snippet and all five components gives an empty `<div>` container each.\n- **DX1 in Chrome:**\n  - The npm snippet (production and development conditions), the script-tag snippet and the React snippet under StrictMode each draw one figure named \"Monthly visitors\" with series-painted marks, and print no console error or warning.\n  - Hydrating the server markup produces no mismatch.\n  - Without `title`, the chart still draws and raises only AX140.\n- **DX8 under CSP:** 8 page variants: {IIFE min, IIFE dev, bundled module prod, bundled module dev} × {stylesheet applied at run time, stylesheet linked by the page}. Each draws all five chart types plus the compact variant and opens tooltips and all five tables. Result: zero violation events, zero reports, zero console errors, no elements created from `<img onerror>` or `<script>` text in titles, series, categories, labels, units or formatters, and `#no-such-chart` is named in the thrown error. Run-time styling adopts exactly one sheet; the linked case adopts none; there are never any `<style>` elements. A negative control (an `insertAdjacentHTML` page) is caught by both instruments.\n  - The exact policy: `default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; report-uri /csp-report`\n- **DX11:** MIT field and LICENSE text in both packages. No runtime dependencies. The shipped JS imports nothing, except `react` and `axylo` from the adapter. Bundling each package's source with the release settings reads only its own `src`, so no `node_modules` code is compiled in. No licence headers in `packages/*/src` or in the shipped files.\n\n### Sizes (`node scripts/size.mjs`, from the packed files, esbuild minify, production condition, gzip level 9)\n\n| entry | min B | js gzip B | css file gzip B | total KiB | target KiB | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| line only (`npm.ts`) | 282,947 | 99,956 | — | 97.61 | 25 | OVER |\n| everything | 283,389 | 100,093 | — | 97.75 | 40 | OVER |\n| script tag (IIFE min + css) | 283,869 | 100,179 | 4,095 | 101.83 | — | no target |\n| React adapter alone | 2,375 | 1,197 | — | 1.17 | 2 | ok |\n\n- `--check` exits 1.\n- The JS already carries the stylesheet string, so the bundler rows do not add the CSS file. Adding it, as the old script did, would add 4,095 B.\n- Breakdown by directory (minified bytes): data 24.3%, core 16.1%, dom 13.5%, theme 8.8%. Largest modules: `core/controller.ts`, `dom/interaction.ts`, `data/store.ts`, `theme/css.ts`.\n- A rebuild from source with the release settings is byte-identical in size to the packed `axylo.js`.\n- **Finding: chart types do not tree-shake.** Line-only saves 137 B gzip compared with everything. Building from source gives the same result (line-only 99,735 B, everything 99,912 B, `validate` only 20,686 B).\n  - The likely cause (inferred, not proven) is that every chart function goes through `createChart(type, …)` in `packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts` / `core/controller.ts`, which reaches all types.\n\n### Failing tests\nNone among the 101. The only failure is `size.mjs --check`, above, for DX7.\n\n### Where the spec was ambiguous, and what I assumed\n1. **DX1 options:** \"no option besides data and fields\" conflicts with AX140, which is a warning (spec 3.5), and with \"no console warnings\". The snippets therefore pass `title`, as the plan 1.1 example does. A test shows the title is not required. `acceptance/matrix.json` DX1 still says \"only data and fields\".\n2. **Script-tag file names:** plan 1.6 calls the script-tag files `axylo.js`/`axylo.min.js`. The build produces `axylo.iife.js`/`axylo.iife.min.js`, and `axylo.js` is the production ESM file. The snippet uses `dist/axylo.iife.min.js`.\n3. **Script-tag URL:** the snippet uses unversioned `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/axylo/dist/...` for a package not yet published. The test routes those URLs to the packed files.\n4. **Script-tag target:** the spec gives no size target for the script-tag row.\n5. **React snippet shape:** it exports a component, which the fixture's `main.tsx` mounts.\n6. **Server markup:** the expected SSR output (an empty container) is taken from plan 1.7, \"create on mount\".\n\n### Lines for files I don't own\nRoot `package.json` scripts: add\n```\n\"test:dist\": \"vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts\",\n\"test:dist:browser\": \"AXYLO_BROWSER=1 vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts\",\n```\nIn the same file, append ` && tsc -p tests/dist` to `typecheck`, and add ` && npm run test:dist && npm run test:dist:browser` to `check` after `test:browser`.\n\n`.gitignore`, after `dist/` (that rule currently ignores all of `tests/dist`; I checked this negation in a scratch repo):\n```\n!/tests/dist/\n/tests/dist/.packed/\n/tests/dist/.out/\n/tests/dist/fixtures/*/node_modules/\n/tests/dist/fixtures/*/example/\n/tests/dist/fixtures/*/.out/\n```\n\n`vitest.config.ts`: no change needed or recommended. The root `include` does not cover `tests/dist`, which is intended: these tests need the pack global setup, so they run through their own config. Adding them to the root config would pack on every `npm test`.\n\n`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, after `- run: npm run build`:\n```yaml\n      - run: npx tsc -p tests/dist\n      - run: npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts\n      - run: npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts\n        env:\n          AXYLO_BROWSER: 1\n```\nThe existing `npm run size` step now measures the packed files. Add `-- --check` only once you want the size targets to gate CI.\n\n### Not verified\n- Only system Chrome on Linux; no other browsers, and no Windows or macOS (the junction and `npm.cmd` paths in `pack.mjs` have never run there).\n- No real `npm install` or registry.\n- No bundler except esbuild: webpack and Rollup are absent, and Vite/rolldown exist only as Vitest's own dependencies.\n- DX10 beyond the three first-chart snippets.\n- Nothing is left running. The headless Chrome visible during my run belonged to the other agent's vitest process.\n\n<!-- Author: Codex gpt-6.2-sol, effort xhigh (observed in the session rollout, thread 01a1ecf1-cc72-7090-a96c-2549eeac7a5b). -->\n\nAdded **494 Node acceptance tests** across 16 files. They exercise all 29 diagnostic codes and provide model evidence for 224 applicable matrix cells. All edits are under `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/`. No contract changes are needed.\n\n| Line | Area | Bar | Scatter | Donut | Compact |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 96 | 87 | 87 | 77 | 57 | 90 |\n\n[Evidence index](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/acceptance/EVIDENCE.json) · [Full report with counts, all 18 failures, likely causes, and spec readings](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/acceptance/REPORT.md)\n\nThe failures cover scatter missing values, date precision and scale domains, automatic tick endpoints, missing x-axis units in aligned tables, AX143 guidance, and compact disclosure text. The assertions remain active.\n\nThe acceptance files passed strict TypeScript checking. Workspace typechecking stopped at TS2367 in the [browser naming test](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a1-names.browser.test.ts:45). Browser rendering, accessibility-tree inspection, assistive-technology rehearsals, and performance budgets remain pending.\n\n```text\n Test Files  7 failed | 9 passed (16)\n      Tests  18 failed | 476 passed (494)\n   Start at  05:52:29\n   Duration  13.01s (tests 89%, transform 5%, import 5%)\n```","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
